# Keep the build context small AND correct.
#
# Without this, `COPY . .` in infra/docker/Dockerfile shipped ~1.2 GB to the
# daemon on every build (node_modules 1.1 GB + build/ + .git) — and worse, it
# copied the HOST's node_modules over the Linux tree that `npm ci` had just
# installed. On a Windows or macOS workstation that means platform-wrong
# binaries inside a linux/amd64 image. It happened to work only because
# Docusaurus is almost entirely pure JS; that is luck, not design.
#
# This matters more here than in most repos: the whole reason docs lives in its
# own repo is that it will fill up with screenshots and video.

node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build artefacts — the image builds its own.
build
.docusaurus
out
dist

# VCS + tooling
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Secrets and local state. auth.json is a Playwright storage-state file with a
# live session in it; .env holds capture/KB credentials. Neither belongs in a
# layer that gets pushed to a registry.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
auth.json

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Repo meta, not site content. Named explicitly rather than `*.md`: this is a
# DOCUMENTATION repo where .md IS the product (docs/ holds 16 of them). A bare
# `*.md` happens to match root-level only, so it works — but it reads like it
# excludes the entire site, and one day someone "fixes" it to `**/*.md` and
# silently ships a site missing a third of its pages.
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
CLAUDE.md

# Large source artwork kept out of the shipped site
brand-assets

# Test + capture output
test-results
playwright-report
tools/output
